DESCRIPTION The structure's weight: load-bearing walls, agents with a scope, teams as members (K06, K16, K17, K18)
CATEGORY Governance
NAMESPACE EtlRGovernanceNS
DEFINE SYSTEM ETL-R AS etl-r-implementations-on-gcp

# Load-bearing (K06): the balance is this repo's first-written function, LMAX style
ASSERT(src_read = written + rejected at the end of every run) # [K06-1]
# the stale mock login killed load mid-run; the queue kept every record (docs/evidence/)
ASSERT(no source record is lost while the Target System is unavailable) # [K06-2]
ASSERT(a 200k run fits on one GKE node: 3 batch jobs, parallelism 1, 4 vCPU) # [K06-3]
# from artefacts.json: a consumer detects completeness without holding a decryption key
ASSERT(the .FLG flag lands outside the encrypted bundle — completeness needs no key) # [K06-4]

# The stacks come from pom.xml and requirements.txt, not from an ADL inventory (K16)
ASSERT(SBOM generated in build) # [K16-1]
ASSERT(no technology inventory in ADL files) # [K16-2]
ASSERT(communication protocols harvested from build SBOM) # [K16-3]

# An agent's scope = one quantum; never "refactor everything" (K17).
# K17's worked example, restated on this repo: an agent is asked to build one of the
# three lanes — implementations/flink/, implementations/flink-jdbc/ or
# implementations/beam-dataflow/ — from spec/ + this ADL
DEFINE AGENT Lane Builder AS the code-generation agent
     SCOPE: exactly one implementation; spec/ and spec/conformance/ stay read-only
     bounded by CLAUDE.md: nothing pushed, nothing billable, commits only when asked
ASSERT(agents cannot add cross-implementation dependencies) # [K17-1]
ASSERT(agents cannot add undeclared database connections) # [K17-2]
ASSERT(agent-generated changes stay within declared structural and operational boundaries) # [K17-3]

# The teams (K18): one maintainer wears every hat today;
# the map exists to read git history and to bound agent scope when more hands arrive
DEFINE PERSON Adrian Balaban AS 50263077+adrian-balaban@users.noreply.github.com
     ROLE: grammarian of the whole lane set — spec first, implementations second
DEFINE AGENT Cline AS the coding agent
     SCOPE: one quantum per task; spec/ and spec/conformance/ stay read-only
DEFINE AGENT dependabot[bot] AS the dependency-update bot
     SCOPE: manifests and workflow pins only — pom.xml, requirements.txt, .github/workflows/
DEFINE TEAM Platform AS the spec and conformance owner
     ASSIGN DOMAIN spec/ spec/conformance/
DEFINE TEAM Flink Lanes AS stream-aligned
     ASSIGN DOMAIN implementations/flink/ implementations/flink-jdbc/
     # the pinned sharing inside the family: mig.common, the Terraform modules, the reactor
DEFINE TEAM Beam Lane AS stream-aligned
     ASSIGN DOMAIN implementations/beam-dataflow/
DEFINE TEAM Target System Mock AS stream-aligned
     ASSIGN DOMAIN implementations/flink/target-system-mock/ implementations/beam-dataflow/apps/target-system-mock/
DEFINE SUPERUSER Team AS the maintainer in emergencies
     DEFINE PERSON Adrian Balaban AS 50263077+adrian-balaban@users.noreply.github.com
          ROLE: any domain, especially teardown and rollback
DEFINE ALUMNI Team AS the git history so far
     # empty: nobody has retired yet (K18 Task 1: one pair of hands produces coherence)

ASSERT(TEAM MEMBERS include PERSONS and AGENTS) # [K18-1]
ASSERT(No commits from anyone other than TEAM MEMBERS) # [K18-2]
ASSERT(TEAM MEMBERS in Stream-Aligned Teams cannot commit files outside their domains) # [K18-3]
ASSERT(Super User Teams can commit files belonging to other teams) # [K18-4]
ASSERT(No merge conflicts within Stream-Aligned Teams caused by AGENTS within the past month) # [K18-5]